%% Owner: docs/15-eval-harness.md — which metric answers which question.
flowchart TB
    classDef evalc fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#c2410c,color:#431407
    classDef io fill:#ffffff,stroke:#111827,color:#111827
    classDef legend fill:#fafafa,stroke:#9ca3af,stroke-dasharray:4 3,color:#374151

    start{"What do you need to know?"}:::io
    found{"Is the evidence<br/>retrieved at all?"}:::io
    where{"How high is it?"}:::io
    all{"Does the answer need<br/>several pieces?"}:::io
    noise{"How much of the context<br/>is noise?"}:::io
    graded{"Do partial matches<br/>matter?"}:::io
    ans{"Is the answer right<br/>and supported?"}:::io
    refuse{"Does it refuse<br/>when it should?"}:::io
    hit["hit@k"]:::evalc
    rec["recall@k<br/>(fraction of items covered)"]:::evalc
    mrr["MRR<br/>(1 / first relevant rank)"]:::evalc
    prec["precision@k"]:::evalc
    ndcg["nDCG@k<br/>(graded, position-discounted)"]:::evalc
    faith["faithfulness · correctness<br/>(LLM judge)"]:::evalc
    abst["abstention precision / recall ·<br/>false-refusal rate · AUROC"]:::evalc
    legend["Legend<br/>white = question you're asking · orange = metric that answers it"]:::legend

    start -->|retrieval| found
    start -->|generation| ans
    start -->|unanswerable questions| refuse
    found -->|any piece| hit
    found -->|all pieces| all
    all -->|yes: multi-hop| rec
    found -->|rank matters| where
    where -->|first hit only| mrr
    where -->|all hits, graded| graded
    graded -->|yes| ndcg
    found -->|context cost| noise
    noise --> prec
    ans --> faith
    refuse --> abst
